{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a796b641589f5bc6e","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_013pY7hYPJnTJRDhzLbprmo4","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-iwlyVP/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-translate-iwlyVP-translated-rust/e867ece2-5670-426a-953e-de496239b763/tasks/a796b641589f5bc6e.output","summary":"Done. `src/utf.rs` is written and type-checks cleanly.\n\n## What was done\n\nWrote exactly one file: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-iwlyVP/translated_rust/src/utf.rs` — a mechanical transliteration of `c_src/src/utf.c` (379 lines).\n\n**10 `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\"` symbols** (confirmed `grep -c 'unsafe(no_mangle)' src/utf.rs` == 10):\n\n| Symbol | Signature |\n|---|---|\n| `jsU_chartorune` | `(*mut Rune, *const c_char) -> c_int` |\n| `jsU_runetochar` | `(*mut c_char, *const Rune) -> c_int` |\n| `jsU_runelen` | `(c_int) -> c_int` |\n| `jsU_isalpharune` | `(Rune) -> c_int` |\n| `jsU_islowerrune` | `(Rune) -> c_int` |\n| `jsU_isupperrune` | `(Rune) -> c_int` |\n| `jsU_tolowerrune` | `(Rune) -> Rune` |\n| `jsU_toupperrune` | `(Rune) -> Rune` |\n| `jsU_tolowerrune_full` | `(Rune) -> *const Rune` |\n| `jsU_toupperrune_full` | `(Rune) -> *const Rune` |\n\nPlus the private `unsafe fn ucd_bsearch(c, t, n, ne) -> *const Rune` and the 10 short-name `pub use` aliases at the end of the file.\n\n## Translation notes\n\n- All `enum` constants (`Bit1..Bit5`, `T1..T5`, `Rune1..Rune4`, `Maskx`, `Testx`, `Bad`) are reproduced as `const c_int` written with the *original C expressions* (e.g. `((1 << (Bitx + 1)) - 1) ^ 0xFF`) rather than pre-computed literals, so the bit-twiddling is verifiable by inspection.\n- The four `goto bad` sites in `chartorune` became a `'bad: { ... break 'bad; ... }` labelled block with the `*rune = Bad; return 1;` tail after it, per the guide's goto pattern.\n- `(uchar)str[i]` → `*(str.offset(i) as *const u8) as c_int`; the overlong-NUL pre-check compares the raw `u8` values directly. The `if(UTFmax >= 4)` guard is kept verbatim (`UTFmax` is `usize` in `jsi.rs`, so the comparison is a const-true).\n- `runetochar`'s stores truncate to `c_char` via `as c_char` exactly where C's implicit `int`→`char` conversion happens; `(char)0xc0`/`(char)0x80` written as `0xc0u8 as c_char` to avoid the out-of-range-literal lint.\n- `nelem(a)/k` → `(a.len() as c_int) / k` against the `src/utfdata.rs` tables (`ucd_alpha1` uses the bare `.len()` with `ne = 1`, matching C).\n- `return c + p[2]` uses `wrapping_add` so the arithmetic cannot panic under a debug profile; values are small so the result is identical either way.\n- `ucd_bsearch` returns `core::ptr::null()` for C's `return 0`, and the `if(p && ...)` guards became `!p.is_null() && ...`, preserving short-circuit order.\n\n## Verification\n\n`cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -i utf` returns **nothing** — zero errors or warnings attributable to `src/utf.rs`.\n\nBecause the build aborts with 90 errors from not-yet-written modules (`E0583` missing module files, plus `E0425` unresolved names in `jsrun.rs`), a clean grep alone would be ambiguous, so I confirmed the file is actually reaching type-check: appending a deliberate type error produced a diagnostic at `src/utf.rs:381`, proving the module is fully compiled rather than skipped. That sentinel was reverted; the file is back to 379 lines with 10 `no_mangle` attributes.\n\nThe remaining crate-wide errors are all in other modules (`jsrun.rs` referencing `js_strictequal`, `jsV_newobject`, etc., and the absent `jsarray.rs`/`jsvalue.rs`/`jsproperty.rs`/… files) and are expected at this stage. No other file was created or modified.","usage":{"total_tokens":48669,"tool_uses":14,"duration_ms":165544},"uuid":"c7354bca-ddfe-41d8-8bd1-5c287ad83d38","session_id":"e867ece2-5670-426a-953e-de496239b763"}
