 part of a larger, already-started translation.\n\nWorking directory: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-iwlyVP/translated_rust\n\nSTEP 1 — Read these files first, fully:\n- TRANSLATION_GUIDE.md   (the rules; follow them exactly)\n- src/jsi.rs             (types/constants/helpers you must use)\n- src/cstd.rs            (libc declarations)\n- src/jserror.rs         (a completed example of the target style)\n- c_src/src/utf.h        (NOTE the `#define` renames!)\n- c_src/src/utf.c        (the file you must translate)\n- src/utfdata.rs         (ALREADY DONE — the Unicode tables; just `use` them)\n\nSTEP 2 — Write EXACTLY ONE file: src/utf.rs   (do not touch any other file)\n\nIt must be a complete, faithful transliteration of c_src/src/utf.c.\n\nRequired exported symbols (all `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn`,\nexact names — these are the macro-renamed linker names from utf.h):\n  jsU_chartorune, jsU_runetochar, jsU_runelen,\n  jsU_isalpharune, jsU_islowerrune, jsU_isupperrune,\n  jsU_tolowerrune, jsU_toupperrune,\n  jsU_tolowerrune_full, jsU_toupperrune_full\n\nSignatures (from utf.h, after macro expansion):\n  int jsU_chartorune(Rune *rune, const char *str);\n  int jsU_runetochar(char *str, const Rune *rune);\n  int jsU_runelen(int c);\n  int jsU_isalpharune(Rune c);  int jsU_islowerrune(Rune c);  int jsU_isupperrune(Rune c);\n  Rune jsU_tolowerrune(Rune c); Rune jsU_toupperrune(Rune c);\n  const Rune *jsU_tolowerrune_full(Rune c);  const Rune *jsU_toupperrune_full(Rune c);\n`Rune` = `crate::jsi::Rune` (= c_int).  UTFmax/Runeself/Runeerror/Runemax constants are in jsi.rs.\n\nALSO: other modules call these functions by their SHORT names. At the end of\nsrc/utf.rs add short-name aliases so callers can use them:\n```rust\npub use self::jsU_chartorune as chartorune;\npub use self::jsU_runetochar as runetochar;\npub use self::jsU_runelen as runelen;\npub use self::jsU_isalpharune as isalpharune;\npub use self::jsU_islowerrune as islowerrune;\npub use self::jsU_isupperrune as isupperrune;\npub use self::jsU_tolowerrune as tolowerrune;\npub use self::jsU_toupperrune as toupperrune;\npub use self::jsU_tolowerrune_full as tolowerrune_full;\npub use self::jsU_toupperrune_full as toupperrune_full;\n```\nThe static helper `ucd_bsearch` stays a private `unsafe fn`.\n`nelem(a)` in C becomes the Rust array's `.len() as c_int`. The tables in\nsrc/utfdata.rs are `pub static ucd_alpha1/alpha2/tolower1/tolower2/toupper1/toupper2/tolower_full/toupper_full: [Rune; N]`.\nReproduce every bit-twiddling detail of chartorune/runetochar exactly (masks,\nTx/Rune1/Rune2/... constants, error cases). Preserve C integer semantics\n(use `as` casts on integers, wrapping where C wraps).\n\nSTEP 3 — Verify your own work:\nRun `cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"utf\\.rs\" | head -50` and fix every\nerror attributable to src/utf.rs. Errors in OTHER modules (which are not written\nyet) are expected — ignore them. Also run\n`grep -c 'unsafe(no_mangle)' src/utf.rs` and confirm it is 10.\n\nSTEP 4 — Report: the list of no_mangle symbols you defined, the file's line\ncount, and any remaining errors in src/utf.rs.","agentId":"a796b641589f5bc6e","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `src/utf.rs` is written and type-checks cleanly.\n\n## What was done\n\nWrote exactly one file: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-iwlyVP/translated_rust/src/utf.rs` — a mechanical transliteration of `c_src/src/utf.c` (379 lines).\n\n**10 `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\"` symbols** (confirmed `grep -c 'unsafe(no_mangle)' src/utf.rs` == 10):\n\n| Symbol | Signature |\n|---|---|\n| `jsU_chartorune` | `(*mut Rune, *const c_char) -> c_int` |\n| `jsU_runetochar` | `(*mut c_char, *const Rune) -> c_int` |\n| `jsU_runelen` | `(c_int) -> c_int` |\n| `jsU_isalpharune` | `(Rune) -> c_int` |\n| `jsU_islowerrune` | `(Rune) -> c_int` |\n| `jsU_isupperrune` | `(Rune) -> c_int` |\n| `jsU_tolowerrune` | `(Rune) -> Rune` |\n| `jsU_toupperrune` | `(Rune) -> Rune` |\n| `jsU_tolowerrune_full` | `(Rune) -> *const Rune` |\n| `jsU_toupperrune_full` | `(Rune) -> *const Rune` |\n\nPlus the private `unsafe fn ucd_bsearch(c, t, n, ne) -> *const Rune` and the 10 short-name `pub use` aliases at the end of the file.\n\n## Translation notes\n\n- All `enum` constants (`Bit1..Bit5`, `T1..T5`, `Rune1..Rune4`, `Maskx`, `Testx`, `Bad`) are reproduced as `const c_int` written with the *original C expressions* (e.g. `((1 << (Bitx + 1)) - 1) ^ 0xFF`) rather than pre-computed literals, so the bit-twiddling is verifiable by inspection.\n- The four `goto bad` sites in `chartorune` became a `'bad: { ... break 'bad; ... }` labelled block with the `*rune = Bad; return 1;` tail after it, per the guide's goto pattern.\n- `(uchar)str[i]` → `*(str.offset(i) as *const u8) as c_int`; the overlong-NUL pre-check compares the raw `u8` values directly. The `if(UTFmax >= 4)` guard is kept verbatim (`UTFmax` is `usize` in `jsi.rs`, so the comparison is a const-true).\n- `runetochar`'s stores truncate to `c_char` via `as c_char` exactly where C's implicit `int`→`char` conversion happens; `(char)0xc0`/`(char)0x80` written as `0xc0u8 as c_char` to avoid the out-of-range-literal lint.\n- `nelem(a)/k` → `(a.len() as c_int) / k` against the `src/utfdata.rs` tables (`ucd_alpha1` uses the bare `.len()` with `ne = 1`, matching C).\n- `return c + p[2]` uses `wrapping_add` so the arithmetic cannot panic under a debug profile; values are small so the result is identical either way.\n- `ucd_bsearch` returns `core::ptr::null()` for C's `return 0`, and the `if(p && ...)` guards became `!p.is_null() && ...`, preserving short-circuit order.\n\n## Verification\n\n`cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -i utf` returns **nothing** — zero errors or warnings attributable to `src/utf.rs`.\n\nBecause the build aborts with 90 errors from not-yet-written modules (`E0583` missing module files, plus `E0425` unresolved names in `jsrun.rs`), a clean grep alone would be ambiguous, so I confirmed the file is actually reaching type-check: appending a deliberate type error produced a diagnostic at `src/utf.rs:381`, proving the module is fully compiled rather than skipped. That sentinel was reverted; the file is back to 379 lines with 10 `no_mangle` attributes.\n\nThe remaining crate-wide errors are all in other modules (`jsrun.rs` referencing `js_strictequal`, `jsV_newobject`, etc., and the absent `jsarray.rs`/`jsvalue.rs`/`jsproperty.rs`/… files) and are expected at this stage. No other file was created or modified."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":165545,"totalTokens":50071,"totalToolUseCount":14,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":311,"cache_read_input_tokens":48208,"output_tokens":1549,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":311},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":5,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":8,"editFileCount":1,"linesAdded":380,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
