erty, jsV_getpropertyx, jsV_getproperty,\n  jsV_setproperty, jsV_delproperty, jsV_newiterator, jsV_nextiterator,\n  jsV_resizearray\nAlso present in jsi.h but *static* in the .c file, so private Rust fns:\n  jsV_getenumproperty, newproperty, lookup, skew, split, insert, freeproperty,\n  unlinkproperty, deleteproperty, itnewnode, itwalk, itflatten\n(`jsV_nextproperty` is declared in jsi.h but not defined — skip it.)\n\nSignatures from jsi.h:\n```c\njs_Object *jsV_newobject(js_State *J, enum js_Class type, js_Object *prototype);\njs_Property *jsV_getownproperty(js_State *J, js_Object *obj, const char *name);\njs_Property *jsV_getpropertyx(js_State *J, js_Object *obj, const char *name, int *own);\njs_Property *jsV_getproperty(js_State *J, js_Object *obj, const char *name);\njs_Property *jsV_setproperty(js_State *J, js_Object *obj, const char *name);\nvoid jsV_delproperty(js_State *J, js_Object *obj, const char *name);\njs_Object *jsV_newiterator(js_State *J, js_Object *obj, int own);\nconst char *jsV_nextiterator(js_State *J, js_Object *iter);\nvoid jsV_resizearray(js_State *J, js_Object *obj, int newlen);\n```\n`enum js_Class` is `c_int` in Rust.\n\nCRITICAL — the AA-tree sentinel:\nThe C file has `static js_Property sentinel = { &sentinel, &sentinel, 0, 0, {{{0},JS_TUNDEFINED}}, NULL, NULL, \"\" };`\nThis exact sentinel is ALREADY provided in src/jsi.rs as\n`pub unsafe fn prop_sentinel() -> *mut js_Property`. Use `prop_sentinel()`\neverywhere C writes `&sentinel`, and compare with `node == prop_sentinel()`.\nOther modules (jsrun.rs, jsgc.rs) rely on this shared sentinel, so do NOT create\nyour own.\n\nOther details:\n- `js_Property` in jsi.rs is\n  `{ left, right: *mut js_Property, level: c_int, atts: c_int, value: js_Value, getter: *mut js_Object, setter: *mut js_Object, name: [c_char;1] }`\n  with `JS_PROPERTY_NAME_OFFSET`. `newproperty` allocates\n  `JS_PROPERTY_NAME_OFFSET + n` bytes and sets fields individually — never\n  assign a whole `js_Property` value.\n  `