ll happens *before* `nextobj` is loaded, as in C.\n- Report line uses libc `snprintf` with the identical format string, `core::mem::size_of_val(&buf)` for `sizeof buf`, `(100u32.wrapping_mul(gtot) / ntot) as c_int` for the percentage, and the ten counters passed `as c_int` (bit-preserving). `js_report` from `crate::jsstate`.\n- `(*J).gcthresh = cvt_u32(remaining as f64 * JS_GCFACTOR);`\n- List surgery uses `core::ptr::addr_of_mut!` for the `prevnext*` back-pointers.\n- `js_freestate` ends with `((*J).alloc.unwrap())((*J).actx, (*J).stack as *mut c_void, 0)` then the same for `J`.\n\n## Verification\n`cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"jsgc\\.rs\"` returns nothing — but only because the build aborts at `src/lib.rs` module resolution: `jsarray, jsboolean, jsbuiltin, jscompile, jsdate, jsdtoa, jsfunction, jsintern, jslex, jsmath, jsnumber, jsobject, json, jsparse, jsproperty, jsregexp, jsrepr, jsstate, jsstring, jsvalue, regexp` (E0583 \"file not found for module\"), so `jsgc.rs` is never type-checked.\n\nTo actually verify, I built a throwaway crate in `$TMPDIR` (since deleted, no repo files touched) that symlinks the real `src/cstd.rs`, `src/jsi.rs`, `src/jsgc.rs` and adds minimal stubs matching the documented signatures of `jsrun::{js_free, js_malloc}`, `jsintern::jsS_freestrings`, `jsstate::js_report`, and `regexp::{Reprog, js_regfreex}`, with `edition = \"2021\"` to match the real `Cargo.toml`. Result: **0 errors, 0 warnings** for `jsgc.rs`.\n\nRemaining errors attributable to `src/jsgc.rs`: none. Its only unresolved references are the four not-yet-written modules it must depend on (`crate::jsrun` exists already; `crate::jsintern`, `crate::jsstate`, `crate::regexp` do not), which will resolve once those files land — provided `regexp.rs` exports `Reprog` and `js_regfreex` as specified in the guide.","usage":{"total_tokens":70565,"tool_uses":18,"duration_ms":223268},"uuid":"7e163dd5-5ec3-41dd-ba99-9fdacd532de4","session_id":"e867ece2-5670-426a-953e-de496239b763"