 from crate::cstd and pass the counters as `c_uint` (C passes them to `%d`, so\n  cast each to `c_int`? NO — C passes `unsigned int` to `%d`; on x86-64 the\n  bits are the same, so pass them as-is via `as c_int` which preserves bits).\n  `100*gtot/ntot` is unsigned int arithmetic — use `wrapping_mul`/`/` on u32\n  (note: division by zero would trap; the C code has the same hazard, keep it,\n  but implement as plain `100u32.wrapping_mul(gtot) / ntot`).\n- `J->gcthresh = remaining * JS_GCFACTOR;` — C computes `unsigned int * double`\n  -> double, then converts to unsigned int. Translate as\n  `(*J).gcthresh = cvt_u32(remaining as f64 * JS_GCFACTOR);`\n- `js_free`, `js_malloc` live in `crate::jsrun`; `jsS_freestrings` in\n  `crate::jsintern`.\n- `J->alloc(J->actx, J->stack, 0)` -> `((*J).alloc.unwrap())((*J).actx, (*J).stack as *mut c_void, 0)`.\n- `obj->u.user.finalize(J, obj->u.user.data)` -> `if let Some(f) = (*obj).u.user.finalize { f(J, (*obj).u.user.data) }`\n  but keep the exact same condition ordering as C\n  (`if (obj->type == JS_CUSERDATA && obj->u.user.finalize)`).\n- `js_report` is in `crate::jsstate`.\n- The declarations of the local variables in js_gc that C declares mid-function\n  (`unsigned int ntot = ...`) can stay in place.\n\nSTEP 3 — Verify: run\n`cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"jsgc\\.rs\" | head -40`\nand fix every error attributable to src/jsgc.rs. Errors in other modules are\nexpected (not written yet).\n\nSTEP 4 — Report the no_mangle symbols defined, line count, and remaining errors.","agentId":"af66a987347a79aed","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote exactly one file: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-iwlyVP/translated_rust/src/jsgc.rs` (397 lines).\n\n## Exported `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\"` symbols\n- `js_gc(J: *mut js_State, report: c_int)`\n- `js_freestate(J: *mut js_State)`\n\n## Private helpers (all 11 `static` C functions translated as private `u