nslation.\n\nWorking directory: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-iwlyVP/translated_rust\n\nSTEP 1 — Read these files first, fully:\n- TRANSLATION_GUIDE.md   (the rules; follow them exactly)\n- src/jsi.rs             (types/constants/helpers you must use)\n- src/cstd.rs            (libc declarations)\n- src/jserror.rs         (a completed example of the target style)\n- c_src/src/regexp.h     (NOTE the `#define` renames!)\n- c_src/src/regexp.c     (the file you must translate — 1277 lines)\n- c_src/src/utf.h        (utf functions; in Rust they live in src/utf.rs with\n                          both the `jsU_*` names and short-name aliases such as\n                          `crate::utf::toupperrune`, `crate::utf::chartorune`)\n\nSTEP 2 — Write EXACTLY ONE file: src/regexp.rs   (do not touch any other file)\n\nRequired exported symbols (`#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn`,\nthese are the macro-renamed linker names from regexp.h):\n  js_regcompx, js_regfreex, js_regcomp, js_regexec, js_regfree\nSignatures:\n```c\nReprog *js_regcompx(void *(*alloc)(void *ctx, void *p, int n), void *ctx,\n                    const char *pattern, int cflags, const char **errorp);\nvoid js_regfreex(void *(*alloc)(void *ctx, void *p, int n), void *ctx, Reprog *prog);\nReprog *js_regcomp(const char *pattern, int cflags, const char **errorp);\nint js_regexec(Reprog *prog, const char *string, Resub *sub, int eflags);\nvoid js_regfree(Reprog *prog);\n```\nIn Rust use\n`pub type ReAlloc = Option<unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn(*mut c_void, *mut c_void, c_int) -> *mut c_void>;`\nfor the alloc callback (it is the same shape as `js_Alloc`).\n\nPublic items other modules need (make them `pub`):\n- `pub struct Reprog { ... }` (opaque to callers, `#[repr(C)]`)\n- `#[repr(C)] pub struct Resub { pub nsub: c_int, pub sub: [ResubSpan; REG_MAXSUB] }`\n  with `#[repr(C)] #[derive(Copy,Clone)] pub struct ResubSpan { pub sp: *const c_char, pub ep: *const c_char }`\n  (this matches the anonymous struct array in regexp.h; keep layout identical)\n- `pub const REG_MAXSUB: usize = 16;`\n- `pub const REG_ICASE: c_int = 1; pub const REG_NEWLINE: c_int = 2; pub const REG_NOTBOL: c_int = 4;`\n- add `pub use` aliases with the short names so other modules can call them:\n  `pub use self::js_regcomp as regcomp;` etc. (regcompx, regfreex, regcomp, regexec, regfree)\n\nIMPORTANT — the `jmp_buf kaboom` in `struct cstate`:\nregexp.c has exactly ONE `setjmp` (in `js_regcompx`, around line 903) and the\n`die()` helper `longjmp`s to it. Do NOT use setjmp/longjmp in Rust. Instead:\n- remove the `kaboom` field\n- make `die()`  `-> !` and have it do\n  `g.error = message; std::panic::panic_any(ReDie);`\n  where `struct ReDie;` is a private marker type in src/regexp.rs\n- replace `if (setjmp(g.kaboom)) { <cleanup>; return NULL; }` with\n  ```rust\n  let r = std::panic::catch_unwind(std::panic::AssertUnwindSafe(|| { /* the code\n      that followed the setjmp, returning the Reprog* */ }));\n  match r {\n      Ok(prog) => prog,\n      Err(p) => { if p.downcast_ref::<ReDie>().is_some() { /* cleanup, set *errorp, return null_mut() */ } else { std::panic::resume_unwind(p) } }\n  }\n  ```\n  Keep the exact same cleanup order and the exact same error strings.\n- also call `crate::jsi::install_panic_hook();` at the top of `js_regcompx` so\n  the panic message is not printed (add\n  `pub struct ReDie;` and register it, OR simpler: reuse the existing suppression\n  by making ReDie's Display irrelevant — just call install_panic_hook() and\n  additionally wrap the payload in `crate::jsi::JsThrow(u64::MAX)`... NO: use\n  your own `ReDie` marker and, to keep stderr clean, panic via\n  `std::panic::panic_any(crate::jsi::JsThrow(u64::MAX))` and downcast to\n  `crate::jsi::JsThrow` checking `.0 == u64::MAX`. This reuses the already\n  installed hook that silences JsThrow payloads.)\n  Call `crate::jsi::install_panic_hook();` at the start of `js_regcompx`.\n\nAll the other