tab funcap funlen vartab varcap varlen\n  filename line lastline gcnext gcmark`.\n- `js_Instruction` is `c_ushort`. `emitraw` etc. do `F->code[F->codelen++] = value`\n  -> `*(*F).code.offset((*F).codelen as isize) = value as js_Instruction; (*F).codelen += 1;`\n- `memcpy(F->code + F->codelen, &num, sizeof num)` style writes of a `double`\n  or `const char*` into the u16 instruction stream must use\n  `((*F).code.offset((*F).codelen as isize) as *mut f64).write_unaligned(num)`\n  and then advance codelen by `sizeof(x)/sizeof(js_Instruction)`.\n  jsrun.rs reads them back with `read_unaligned`, so keep the same layout.\n- `js_realloc`/`js_malloc`/`js_free` from crate::jsrun; `js_intern` from\n  crate::jsintern; `jsV_numbertostring`, `js_itoa` from crate::jsvalue if used.\n- `J->gcfun` / `fun->gcnext` list linkage in `newfun`.\n- `assert(...)` -> drop.\n- Preserve the exact order of emitted opcodes and the exact jump patching\n  arithmetic — the byte code layout must be identical.\n\nSTEP 3 — Verify: run\n`cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"jscompile\\.rs\" | head -60`\nand fix every error attributable to src/jscompile.rs. Errors in other modules\n(not written yet) are expected. If the build aborts before type-checking\nbecause other modules are missing (E0583), create a THROWAWAY crate under\n`$TMPDIR` that includes only the modules that exist plus stubs, to type-check\nyour file — and delete it afterwards. Never add stub files to src/.\n\nSTEP 4 — Report the no_mangle symbols defined, line count, and remaining errors.","uuid":"0aca8359-dd33-45bb-bf90-a596dd3848f6","session_id":"e867ece2-5670-426a-953e-de496239b763"}
