ARK`, and that plus `URIRESERVED \"#\"`), with the original macro definitions retained as comments.\n- `char`-vs-`unsigned char` sign behaviour preserved: `(unsigned char)*str++` → `as u8 as c_int`, while `a = *str++` (plain `char`) → `as c_int` (sign-extending).\n- `jsB_init` keeps the C ordering, including `jsB_initdate` **before** `jsB_initerror` (the task brief listed date last; the C file is authoritative and was followed), and the three `js_defglobal` calls for `NaN`/`Infinity`/`undefined` before the eight `jsB_globalf` registrations.\n- `js_regcompx((*J).alloc, (*J).actx, c\"(?:)\", 0, null_mut())` result cast to `*mut c_void` for `u.r.prog`; `regexp::ReAlloc` coerces from `js_Alloc` since both are the same fn-pointer shape.\n\n## Verification\n`cargo build --release` in the real crate aborts before type-checking with 12 `E0583` errors for not-yet-written modules (`jsarray`, `jsboolean`, `jscompile`, `jsdate`, `jsfunction`, `jslex`, `jsmath`, `jsnumber`, `jsobject`, `json`, `jsparse`, `jsregexp`, `jsstring`) — no `jsbuiltin.rs` lines appear. To actually type-check, I built a throwaway crate under `$TMPDIR` symlinking the 16 existing modules plus minimal stubs for the missing ones: **`src/jsbuiltin.rs` compiles with zero errors and zero warnings**. A deliberate-error sanity check confirmed the throwaway crate really type-checks the sources rather than short-circuiting. The throwaway crate has been deleted; no stub files were added to `src/`.\n\n**Remaining errors attributable to `src/jsbuiltin.rs`: none.**","usage":{"total_tokens":79943,"tool_uses":23,"duration_ms":267747},"uuid":"86ec312c-50a4-4ec3-8a3c-a82525ee7dba","session_id":"e867ece2-5670-426a-953e-de496239b763"}
