5a3ce00-f5ae-4adf-8120-035b886ba5f8","timestamp":"2026-08-22T15:30:47.731Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are translating one C file of the MuJS interpreter into Rust as part of a larger, already-started translation.\n\nWorking directory: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-iwlyVP/translated_rust\n\nSTEP 1 — Read these files first, fully:\n- TRANSLATION_GUIDE.md   (the rules; follow them exactly)\n- src/jsi.rs             (types/constants/helpers you must use — js_Ast,\n                          js_JumpList, AST_*/EXP_*/STM_* and TK_* constants)\n- src/cstd.rs, src/macros.rs\n- src/jsrun.rs and src/jsvalue.rs (completed examples of the target style)\n- c_src/src/jsparse.c    (the file you must translate — 1065 lines)\n- c_src/src/jsi.h        (declarations)\n\nSTEP 2 — Write EXACTLY ONE file: src/jsparse.rs   (do not touch any other file)\n\nRequired exported symbols (`#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn`):\n  jsP_parsefunction, jsP_parse, jsP_freeparse\nSignatures (jsi.h):\n```c\njs_Ast *jsP_parsefunction(js_State *J, const char *filename, const char *params, const char *body);\njs_Ast *jsP_parse(js_State *J, const char *filename, const char *source);\nvoid jsP_freeparse(js_State *J);\n```\nEvery other function in jsparse.c is `static` -> private Rust `unsafe fn` with\nthe same name. There are many; translate ALL of them:\nadditive, arguments, arrayelement, arrayliteral, assignment, bitand, bitor,\nbitxor, block, callexp, caseclause, caselist, conditional, equality, expression,\nforexpression, forstatement, funbody, fundec, funexp, funstm, identifier,\nidentifiername, identifieropt, jsP_error, jsP_foldconst, jsP_freejumps,\njsP_list, jsP_newnode, jsP_newnumnode, jsP_newstrnode, jsP_next,\njsP_setnumnode, jsP_warning, logand, logor, memberexp, multiplicative, newexp,\nobjectliteral, parameters, postfix, primary, propassign, propname, relational,\nscript, scriptelement, semicolon, shift, statement, statementlist, toint32,\ntouint32, unary, vardec, vardeclist.\nNOTE: `arguments` and `script` are fine as Rust fn names.\n\nThe two variadic statics become macros at the top of the file:\n```rust\nmacro_rules! jsP_error {\n    ($J:expr, $fmt:expr $(, $a:expr)*) => {{\n        let mut msgbuf = [0 as c_char; 256];\n        let mut buf = [0 as c_char; 512];\n        snprintf(msgbuf.as_mut_ptr(), 256, $fmt $(, $a)*);\n        snprintf(buf.as_mut_ptr(), 256, c\"%s:%d: \".as_ptr(), (*$J).filename, (*$J).lexline);\n        strcat(buf.as_mut_ptr(), msgbuf.as_ptr());\n        crate::jserror::js_newsyntaxerror($J, buf.as_ptr());\n        crate::jsrun::js_throw($J)\n    }};\n}\nmacro_rules! jsP_warning {\n    ($J:expr, $fmt:expr $(, $a:expr)*) => {{\n        let mut msg = [0 as c_char; 256];\n        let mut buf = [0 as c_char; 512];\n        snprintf(msg.as_mut_ptr(), 256, $fmt $(, $a)*);\n        snprintf(buf.as_mut_ptr(), 512, c\"%s:%d: warning: %s\".as_ptr(), (*$J).filename, (*$J).lexline, msg.as_ptr());\n        crate::jsstate::js_report($J, buf.as_ptr());\n    }};\n}\n```\n`jsP_error!` diverges (`-> !`).\n\nThe recursion-guard macros become Rust macros too:\n```rust\nmacro_rules! INCREC { ($J:expr) => { { (*$J).astdepth += 1; if (*$J).astdepth > JS_ASTLIMIT { jsP_error!($J, c\"too much recursion\".as_ptr()); } } } }\nmacro_rules! DECREC { ($J:expr) => { (*$J).astdepth -= 1 } }\n```\n`SAVEREC()` / `POPREC()` -> `let SAVE = (*J).astdepth;` / `(*J).astdepth = SAVE;`\n(declare the local explicitly at the exact place the C macro expands).\n\nOther details:\n- `js_Ast` fields in Rust: `type_`, `line`, `parent`, `a`, `b`, `c`, `d`,\n  `number`, `string`, `jumps`, `casejump`, `gcnext`. `js_JumpList` fields:\n  `type_`, `inst`, `next`.\n- `LIST(x)` / helper macros in jsparse.c: expand them faithfully.\n- Lexer: `use crate::jslex::*;` (jsY_lex, jsY_initlex, jsY_tokenstring,\n  jsY_iswhite, jsY_isnewline, ... ). `J->lookahead`, `J->text`, `J->number`,\n  `J->lexline`, `J->astdepth`, `J->gcast`, `J->newline` are js_State fields.\n- `js_malloc`, `js_free` from crate::jsrun; `js_intern` from crate::jsintern;\n  `jsV_numbertostring`/`js_strtol` etc. from crate::jsvalue if referenced.\n- `toint32`/`touint32` statics in this file: they are the parser's own copies;\n  translate as written (watch the double->int casts: use `cvt_i32`/`cvt_u32`).\n- Any `static const char *futurewords[]`-style tables: same treatment as\n  described for jslex — keep the exact order, use `&CStr` statics and\n  materialise `*const c_char` arrays where a `*const *const c_char` is needed.\n\nSTEP 3 — Verify: run\n`cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"jsparse\\.rs\" | head -60`\nand fix every error attributable to src/jsparse.rs. Errors in other modules\n(not written yet) are expected. If the build aborts before type-checking\nbecause other modules are missing (E0583), create a THROWAWAY crate under\n`$TMPDIR` that includes only the modules that exist plus stubs, to type-check\nyour file — and delete it afterwards. Never add stub files to src/.\n\nSTEP 4 — Report the no_mangle symbols defined, line count, and remaining errors.","agentId":"a224c6876623f3254","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `src/jsparse.rs` written (1370 lines) — the only file I touched. Throwaway type-check crate created under `$TMPDIR` and deleted afterwards.\n\n## Exported symbols (`#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn`)\n\n- `jsP_parse(J, filename, source) -> *mut js_Ast`\n- `jsP_parsefunction(J, filename, params, body) -> *mut js_Ast`\n- `jsP_freeparse(J)`\n\nVerified via `nm` on the throwaway rlib: exactly those three appear as `T jsP_*`.\n\n## Private items\n\nAll 55 `static` C functions translated as private `unsafe fn` with identical names: `additive, arguments, arrayelement, arrayliteral, assignment, bitand, bitor, bitxor, block, callexp, caseclause, caselist, conditional, equality, expression, forexpression, forstatement, funbody, fundec, funexp, funstm, identifier, identifiername, identifieropt, jsP_foldconst, jsP_freejumps, jsP_list, jsP_newnode, jsP_newnumnode, jsP_newstrnode, jsP_next, jsP_setnumnode, logand, logor, memberexp, multiplicative, newexp, objectliteral, parameters, postfix, primary, propassign, propname, relational, script, scriptelement, semicolon, shift, statement, statementlist, toint32, touint32, unary, vardec, vardeclist`.\n\nMacros (mirroring the C preprocessor macros / variadics): `jsP_error!` (diverges, `-> !`), `jsP_warning!`, `jsP_expect!`, `INCREC!`, `DECREC!`, `LIST!`, `NODE0!`..`NODE4!` (the `EXP*`/`STM*` families, with the node-type constant spelled at the use site). `jsP_accept` is an `#[inline] unsafe fn` returning `bool`. `SAVEREC()`/`POPREC()` are `let SAVE = (*J).astdepth;` / `(*J).astdepth = SAVE;` at the exact expansion points.\n\n## Notable translation decisions\n\n- The seven `goto loop` functions (`memberexp, callexp, multiplicative, additive, shift, relational, equality`) became `loop { INCREC!; line = …; if accept { …; continue; } … break; }` followed by `POPREC`.\n- Constant folding integer semantics: `~toint32(x)` → `(!toint32(x)) as f64`; `EXP_SHL` → `(((toint32(x) as c_uint) << (touint32(y) & 0x1F)) as c_int) as f64` (wrapping, matching gcc's `shll`); `EXP_SHR` arithmetic `i32 >> u32`; `EXP_USHR` unsigned `u32 >> u32` then unsigned→double. `toint32`'s two `return d;`/`return d - two32;` double→int casts use `cvt_i32`.\n- `match (*node).type_` uses the `jsi.rs` consts as constant patterns; I explicitly re-checked with `--force-warn unreachable_patterns` (crate-level `#![allow]` would otherwise have masked a mis-resolution into a binding) — no warnings, so they do match by value.\n- Argument-evaluation-order audit: every nested `jsP_newnode` call site was checked; the C code only ever passes already-computed locals alongside one nested call, so gcc's right-to-left order and Rust's left-to-right produce the same AST and the same `J->gcast` chain order (including `funstm`'s double use of `a`, where `a->parent` ends up on the `EXP_VAR` node either way).\n\n## Remaining errors\n\nZero attributable to `src/jsparse.rs`. `cargo build --release` still reports 9 errors, all `E0583` \"file not found for module\" for modules not yet written (`jscompile, jsdate, jslex, jsmath, jsnumber, jsobject, jsboolean, jsfunction, jsstring, jsarray, jsbuiltin, jsregexp, json, jsrepr` — grouped into 9 diagnostics). `jsparse.rs` type-checked cleanly in isolation against stubs for `jslex` (`jsY_lex`, `jsY_initlex`, `jsY_tokenstring`), `jsintern`, `jsrun`, `jserror`, `jsstate`; the only warnings were benign `unused_mut`/`unused_assignments` on locals that mirror C's uninitialized declarations, which `lib.rs` allows globally."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":425904,"totalTokens":109241,"totalToolUseCount":17,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1119,"cache_read_input_tokens":106555,"output_tokens":1564,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1119},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":5,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":11,"editFileCount":1,"linesAdded":1371,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
