src/cstd.rs, src/macros.rs\n- src/jsrun.rs and src/jsvalue.rs (completed examples of the target style)\n- c_src/src/jslex.c      (the file you must translate — 881 lines)\n- c_src/src/jsi.h        (declarations, TK_* constants — already in src/jsi.rs)\n\nSTEP 2 — Write EXACTLY ONE file: src/jslex.rs   (do not touch any other file)\n\nRequired exported symbols (`#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn`,\nthe non-static functions of jslex.c):\n  jsY_iswhite, jsY_isnewline, jsY_ishex, jsY_tohex, jsY_tokenstring,\n  jsY_findword, jsY_initlex, jsY_lex, jsY_lexjson\nSignatures (jsi.h):\n```c\nint jsY_iswhite(int c);  int jsY_isnewline(int c);\nint jsY_ishex(int c);    int jsY_tohex(int c);\nconst char *jsY_tokenstring(int token);\nint jsY_findword(const char *s, const char **list, int num);\nvoid jsY_initlex(js_State *J, const char *filename, const char *source);\nint jsY_lex(js_State *J);\nint jsY_lexjson(js_State *J);\n```\nEverything else in the file is `static` and becomes a private `unsafe fn`:\njsY_error, jsY_findkeyword, jsY_isdec, jsY_isidentifierpart,\njsY_isidentifierstart, jsY_lexx, jsY_next, jsY_unescape, isnlthcontext,\nisregexpcontext, lexcomment, lexescape, lexhex, lexjsonescape, lexjsonnumber,\nlexjsonstring, lexlinecomment, lexnumber, lexregexp, lexstring, textend,\ntextinit, textpush.\n\nThe variadic `static void jsY_error(js_State *J, const char *fmt, ...)` must\nbecome a macro (place it near the top of the file):\n```rust\nmacro_rules! jsY_error {\n    ($J:expr, $fmt:expr $(, $a:expr)*) => {{\n        let mut msgbuf = [0 as c_char; 256];\n        let mut buf = [0 as c_char; 512];\n        snprintf(msgbuf.as_mut_ptr(), 256, $fmt $(, $a)*);\n        snprintf(buf.as_mut_ptr(), 256, c\"%s:%d: \".as_ptr(), (*$J).filename, (*$J).lexline);\n        strcat(buf.as_mut_ptr(), msgbuf.as_ptr());\n        crate::jserror::js_newsyntaxerror($J, buf.as_ptr());\n        crate::jsrun::js_throw($J)\n    }};\n}\n```\n(`snprintf(buf, 256, ...)` — note the C code passes 256 not `sizeof buf`; keep it.)\nUse `jsY_error!(J, c\"...\".as_ptr(), args...)` at every call site. It diverges.\n\nOther details:\n- The keyword table `static const char *keywords[]` must be\n  `static keywords: [*const c_char; N]` — but a `static` array of raw pointers\n  needs `unsafe impl Sync` or a const fn; the simplest correct approach is\n  ```rust\n  static KEYWORDS: [&core::ffi::CStr; N] = [c\"break\", c\"case\", ...];\n  ```\n  and then build the `*const c_char` list where needed. `jsY_findkeyword` calls\n  `jsY_findword(s, keywords, nelem(keywords))`; since `jsY_findword` takes\n  `*const *const c_char`, materialise a local\n  `let list: [*const c_char; N] = core::array::from_fn(|i| KEYWORDS[i].as_ptr());`\n  inside `jsY_findkeyword` (a small stack array, no observable difference), or\n  use a lazily initialised `static mut`. Whichever you choose, the *order* of\n  the keyword strings must be identical to the C table, since jsY_findword\n  does a binary search and returns `TK_BREAK + i`.\n- `J->lexbuf` is `js_LexBuf { text: *mut c_char, len: c_int, cap: c_int }`.\n- `J->lexchar`, `J->lexline`, `J->source`, `J->filename`, `J->text`,\n  `J->number`, `J->lasttoken`, `J->newline` are all fields of `js_State`.\n- utf functions: `use crate::utf::{chartorune, runetochar, runelen, isalpharune};`\n  (`Rune`, `UTFmax`, `Runeerror` come from jsi.rs).\n- `js_realloc`, `js_free`, `js_malloc`, `js_intern` (crate::jsintern),\n  `js_strtod`/`js_grisu2` (crate::jsdtoa), `js_strtol`/`js_stringtofloat`\n  (crate::jsvalue) as needed.\n- The `EOF`-ish sentinel: C uses `#define EOF (-1)` from stdio — define\n  `const EOF: c_int = -1;` locally if used.\n- `strtod`-style number parsing: use exactly the same helper the C code uses.\n- Preserve every `switch` fallthrough explicitly, and the exact order of tests.\n\nSTEP 3 — Verify: run\n`cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"jslex\\.rs\" | head -60`\nand fix every error attributable to src/jslex.rs. Errors in other modules\n(not written yet) are expected. If the build aborts before type-checking\nbecause other modules are missing (E0583), create a THROWAWAY crate under\n`$TMPDIR` that includes only the modules that exist plus stubs, to type-check\nyour file — and delete it afterwards. Never add stub files to src/.\n\nSTEP 4 — Report the no_mangle symbols defined, line count, and remaining errors.","agentId":"a9fe9a5a6af93a2b0","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`src/jslex.rs` is written and verified. Nothing else was touched.\n\n## Exported (`#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\"`) symbols — 9, all confirmed as `T` in `nm` output\n\n`jsY_iswhite`, `jsY_isnewline`, `jsY_ishex`, `jsY_tohex`, `jsY_tokenstring`, `jsY_findword`, `jsY_initlex`, `jsY_lex`, `jsY_lexjson`\n\n## Private helpers (all 23 statics from jslex.c)\n\n`jsY_findkeyword`, `jsY_isdec`, `jsY_isidentifierpart`, `jsY_isidentifierstart`, `jsY_lexx`, `jsY_next`, `jsY_unescape`, `isnlthcontext`, `isregexpcontext`, `lexcomment`, `lexescape`, `lexhex`, `lexjsonescape`, `lexjsonnumber`, `lexjsonstring`, `lexlinecomment`, `lexnumber`, `lexregexp`, `lexstring`, `textend`, `textinit`, `textpush` — plus `jsY_error!` as a macro near the top (exact form given in the task), and `jsY_accept!` / `jsY_expect!` macros mirroring the C `#define`s. The C `isalpha`/`isdigit`/`ishex` fallback macros became private `#[inline] fn`s (jsi.h does not include `<ctype.h>`, so the local macro definitions are the ones in effect).\n\n## Line count\n1079 lines.\n\n## Remaining errors attributable to src/jslex.rs\nNone.\n\n`cargo build --release` in the real crate still aborts with 8 × `E0583` (`jscompile`, `jsdate`, `jsmath`, `jsnumber`, `json`, `jsregexp`, `jsrepr`, `jsstring` not written yet), which prevents type-checking entirely. To verify, I built a throwaway crate under `$TMPDIR` containing the **real** current `src/*.rs` plus minimal stubs for only those 8 modules: it compiled with **zero errors and zero warnings**, and the `.so` exported all 9 `jsY_*` symbols. The throwaway crate has been deleted; no stub files were added to `src/`.\n\n## Correctness checks worth noting\n- The 313-entry `tokenstring` table is represented as `static TOKENSTRING: [Option<&CStr>; 313]` (`NULL` → `None`, matching `if (tokenstring[token])`). I verified all 313 entries **byte-for-byte** against the C source by dumping `jsY_tokenstring(0..312)` from a compiled build and comparing against a C-escape-decoded parse of `c_src/src/jslex.c`: zero mismatches. This includes the two quirky literals the C file contains — index 39 is `'\\''` and index 92 is `''` (the C source writes `\"'\\'\"`, i.e. the backslash entry renders as two apostrophes, not a backslash). That oddity is preserved verbatim.\n- `KEYWORDS` order verified identical to the C table and confirmed sorted, so the `jsY_findword` binary search and `TK_BREAK + i` arithmetic remain valid. `jsY_findkeyword` materialises a local `[*const c_char; 29]` from the static `CStr`s; the pointers stored into `J->text` point at promoted statics (program lifetime), not the stack array.\n- `switch` statements were transliterated as ordered `if`/`else if` chains so the implicit \"no case matched → continue after the switch\" behaviour in `jsY_lexx` is preserved exactly; the `'\\''`/`'\"'` shared case and the `lexescape` `EOF`/`lexjsonescape` `default` noreturn fallthroughs are handled explicitly. `jsY_unescape`'s `goto error` became a labelled block."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":538630,"totalTokens":121187,"totalToolUseCount":29,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":257,"cache_read_input_tokens":119594,"output_tokens":1333,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":257},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"st