{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"ae2532bb46f55ffef","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_018QJt4GzLmfNZvmPAyFjfVZ","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-iwlyVP/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-translate-iwlyVP-translated-rust/e867ece2-5670-426a-953e-de496239b763/tasks/ae2532bb46f55ffef.output","summary":"Done. Wrote exactly two files; no other files touched.\n\n## Files\n\n**`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-iwlyVP/translated_rust/src/jsnumber.rs`** — 338 lines (C source: 198)\n- `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` symbol: **`jsB_initnumber`** (only one, matching the sole non-static function in `jsnumber.c`)\n- Private: `jsB_new_Number`, `jsB_Number`, `Np_valueOf`, `Np_toString`, `Np_toFixed`, `Np_toExponential`, `Np_toPrecision` (all `unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn`, registered via `Some(...)`), plus `numtostr` as a plain `unsafe fn`.\n\n**`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-iwlyVP/translated_rust/src/jsmath.rs`** — 195 lines (C source: 194)\n- `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` symbol: **`jsB_initmath`** (only one)\n- Private: all 18 `Math_*` `js_CFunction`s as `unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn`; `Math_init_random` and `jsM_round` as plain `unsafe fn` (their addresses are never taken).\n\n## Verification\n\n`cargo build --release` on the real crate aborts with 5 × `E0583` for the not-yet-written modules `jsdate`, `json`, `jsregexp`, `jsrepr`, `jsstring`. I type-checked via a throwaway crate under `$TMPDIR` (copy of `src/` + minimal stubs for those 5 modules), which **compiled clean with zero errors and zero warnings**, and `nm` confirmed `T jsB_initmath` / `T jsB_initnumber` in the resulting `libmujs.so`. The throwaway crate was deleted. Grepping the real build for `jsnumber.rs|jsmath.rs` yields nothing.\n\n## Fidelity notes worth flagging\n\n- **`numtostr` uses `sprintf`, not `snprintf`.** The C code is `sprintf(buf, fmt, w, n)` into `char buf[50]`, then `sprintf(e, \"e%+d\", exp)` overwriting in place. I used `sprintf` verbatim rather than `snprintf` so truncation behaviour is identical. The exponent fix-up in this version of MuJS is `atoi(e+1)` + `sprintf(e, \"e%+d\", exp)` — there is no `js_fmtexp` call in `jsnumber.c`, so none was introduced.\n- **`atoi` is not declared in `src/cstd.rs`.** Since I may not edit `cstd.rs`, I added a local `extern \"C\" { fn atoi(...) -> c_int; }` block in `jsnumber.rs`.\n- **`jsM_round` returns `+0.0`, not `-0.0`, for `x in [-0.5, 0)`.** The C source reads `return -0;` — that is the *integer* constant `0` negated, which converts to `+0.0`. Reproducing this faithfully (with a comment) rather than \"fixing\" it to `-0.0` was required for byte-identical behaviour; this is the one place a naive translation would silently diverge.\n- **`Np_toString`'s `js_try` block** uses the raw-pointer sharing pattern from the guide for `sb`, `ndigits` and `point` (all mutated inside the body, `sb` read in the handler). The three `x--`/`x++` post-inc/dec loop conditions were unfolded explicitly so the increment still happens on the exiting iteration.\n- **`Math_random`** keeps the C `(uint64_t)J->seed * 48271 % 0x7fffffff` widening (via `wrapping_mul` on `u64`), and `Math_init_random` keeps `time(NULL) + 123` as the entropy source with the three xorshift steps on 32-bit `c_uint`.\n- Property-definition order in both `jsB_init*` functions, and all `jsB_propn` literals, are byte-for-byte as in C.","usage":{"total_tokens":101830,"tool_uses":29,"duration_ms":650554},"uuid":"9c4e5dbc-1983-4136-ab19-67854ff5854b","session_id":"e867ece2-5670-426a-953e-de496239b763"}
