e them). C's `m.sub[i].sp` -> `m.sub[i].sp`.\n  Create it with `core::mem::zeroed()` (C leaves it uninitialised; zeroing is\n  harmless because `regexec` fills it, and Rust must not read uninit memory).\n- `js_toregexp` (crate::jsrun) returns `*mut js_Regexp`; `(*re).prog` is\n  `*mut c_void` and must be cast to `*mut crate::regexp::Reprog` for `regexec`.\n- `js_Buffer` output uses `js_putc`/`js_puts`/`js_putm` from `crate::jsintern`\n  plus the `if (js_try(J)) { js_free(J, sb); js_throw(J); }` idiom -> `js_do_try`\n  with the volatile/raw-pointer pattern from the guide.\n- utf: `use crate::utf::{chartorune, runetochar, runelen, tolowerrune, toupperrune, tolowerrune_full, toupperrune_full};`\n- errors: `js_rangeerror!`, `js_typeerror!`, `js_error!` macros.\n- double->int casts: `cvt_i32` (see the guide).\n- `js_pushlstring`, `js_pushstring`, `js_pushnumber`, `js_getlength`\n  (crate::jsarray), `js_setindex`, `js_concat`, `js_newarray` etc. as needed.\n- `qsort`/`memcmp`/`strcmp`/`strstr`/`strlen`/`memcpy` from crate::cstd.\n- Preserve the exact order of property definitions in `jsB_initstring`.\n\nSTEP 3 — Verify: run\n`cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"jsstring\\.rs\" | head -60`\nand fix every error attributable to src/jsstring.rs. Errors in other modules\n(jsdate, jsregexp, json, jsrepr may still be missing) are expected. If the build\naborts before type-checking because other modules are missing (E0583), create a\nTHROWAWAY crate under `$TMPDIR` with stubs for the missing modules to\ntype-check your file — and delete it afterwards. Never add stub files to src/.\n\nSTEP 4 — Report the no_mangle symbols defined, line count, and remaining errors."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01S9g6qhAdQd3suQAUxnQ1kj","session_id":"e867ece2-5670-426a-953e-de496239b763","uuid":"08c94b9b-0e67-4cde-80b0-020b9cde1a10","timestamp":"2026-08-22T15:36:39.689Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate jsstring.c to Rust"}
