_char` per the guide's `js_do_try` idiom; handler does `js_free` + `js_throw`, tail does `js_free`.\n- Property definition order in `jsB_initregexp` preserved: `toString`, `test`, `exec`, then `js_newcconstructor` + `js_defglobal`.\n- `Resub` via `core::mem::zeroed()`; `js_utfptrtoidx` imported from `crate::jsstring`.\n\n## Verification\n`cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep jsregexp.rs` produces **no output** — zero errors or warnings attributable to my file.\n\nThe real crate still aborts at E0583 for the not-yet-written `jsdate` and `jsstring` modules (`json` and `jsrepr` appeared during my run, presumably from parallel agents). To type-check, I built a throwaway crate in `$TMPDIR/tc_jsregexp` containing the real `src/*.rs` plus minimal stubs for the four then-missing modules; that crate compiled cleanly (`Finished release profile`), which exercised full type-checking of `jsregexp.rs`. The throwaway crate has been deleted, and no stub files were added to `src/`.","usage":{"total_tokens":74086,"tool_uses":26,"duration_ms":216155},"uuid":"1610d54a-2eff-4f5c-9cf7-88d3f44e4a6a","session_id":"e867ece2-5670-426a-953e-de496239b763"}
