{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"aaeff24a41a7594b8","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01RCFgzVdWjNNrb4NUwYP9MT","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-iwlyVP/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-translate-iwlyVP-translated-rust/e867ece2-5670-426a-953e-de496239b763/tasks/aaeff24a41a7594b8.output","summary":"Done. Wrote exactly one file: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-iwlyVP/translated_rust/src/jsrepr.rs` (362 lines).\n\n## Exported `no_mangle` symbols (verified as `T` in the built cdylib)\n- `js_repr(J: *mut js_State, idx: c_int)`\n- `js_torepr(J: *mut js_State, idx: c_int) -> *const c_char`\n- `js_tryrepr(J: *mut js_State, idx: c_int, error: *const c_char) -> *const c_char`\n\nAll three are `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\"`, matching the `mujs.h` declarations at lines 242-244.\n\n## Private statics translated (plain `unsafe fn`, no address taken)\n`reprnum`, `reprstr`, `reprident`, `reprobject`, `reprarray`, `reprfun`, `reprvalue` (recursive, as in C), plus the file's own ASCII-only `isalpha`/`isdigit` fallback macros as `#[inline] unsafe fn`.\n\n## Notable translation decisions\n- `jsi.h` does **not** include `<ctype.h>`, so jsrepr.c's `#ifndef isalpha`/`#ifndef isdigit` fallback macros are the ones actually compiled. Translated as ASCII-only helpers (behaviourally identical to glibc's C-locale versions for both ASCII and negative/high-bit `char` values, so no observable divergence).\n- jsrepr.c calls `js_try(J)` directly (not a local `js_ptry` copy), so both `js_repr` and `js_tryrepr` use `js_do_try` per the guide. `js_repr`'s `sb` is shared with the handler via the raw-pointer pattern (`let sbp = &mut sb as *mut *mut js_Buffer`) since the C handler reads it after a throw; the handler does `js_free` + `js_throw`, the tail does `js_free`.\n- `reprstr`'s `switch (c)` became a `match` on hex literals (Rust patterns can't contain `b'\"' as Rune` casts) with comments naming each original character; the `static const char *HEX` became a local `c\"0123456789ABCDEF\".as_ptr()`.\n- `reprvalue`'s C `switch` had `default:` **first**; in Rust it is the last `_ =>` arm calling `reprobject`, with `JS_CFUNCTION | JS_CSCRIPT` sharing the `reprfun` arm.\n- Every format/output string is byte-identical, including the truncated-looking `\"[iterator \"` for `JS_CITERATOR` (that is what the C source contains — not a typo I introduced).\n\n## Build status\n`cargo build --release` on the real crate still aborts with three `E0583` errors for `src/jsdate.rs`, `src/json.rs`, and `src/jsstring.rs`, which do not exist yet — this is pre-type-check, so it reports nothing about any module.\n\nTo type-check my file I built a throwaway crate under `$TMPDIR/jsrepr_tc` (full `src/` copy plus three minimal stub modules). It compiled with **zero errors and zero warnings across the whole crate**, and `nm` confirmed the three symbols. The throwaway crate has been deleted; no stub files were added to `src/`. Filtering the real build for `jsrepr.rs` yields no lines.","usage":{"total_tokens":113786,"tool_uses":21,"duration_ms":230364},"uuid":"cf8957e0-6585-41ba-835d-0491e7f3d5f7","session_id":"e867ece2-5670-426a-953e-de496239b763"}
