d   (the rules; follow them exactly)\n- src/jsi.rs, src/cstd.rs (note: `tm`, `timeval`, `time`, `mktime`, `gmtime`,\n                           `localtime`, `gettimeofday` are already declared\n                           there), src/macros.rs\n- src/jsrun.rs, src/jsvalue.rs (completed examples of the style)\n- c_src/src/jsdate.c     (the file you must translate — 861 lines)\n\nSTEP 2 — Write EXACTLY ONE file: src/jsdate.rs   (do not touch any other file)\n\nRequired exported symbols (`#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn`):\n  jsB_initdate -> `void jsB_initdate(js_State *J)`\nPrivate (static in C), same names — translate ALL of them:\n  Now, LocalTZA, DaylightSavingTA, LocalTime, UTC, Day, TimeWithinDay,\n  DaysInYear, DayFromYear, TimeFromYear, YearFromTime, InLeapYear,\n  DayWithinYear, MonthFromTime, DateFromTime, WeekDay, HourFromTime,\n  MinFromTime, SecFromTime, msFromTime, MakeTime, MakeDay, MakeDate, TimeClip,\n  pmod, toint, parseDateTime, fmttime, fmtdate, fmtdatetime, js_todate,\n  js_setdate, D_parse, D_UTC, D_now, jsB_Date, jsB_new_Date, and all the\n  `Dp_*` methods (Dp_valueOf, Dp_getTime, Dp_toString, Dp_toDateString,\n  Dp_toTimeString, Dp_toUTCString, Dp_toISOString, Dp_toJSON, Dp_getFullYear,\n  Dp_getMonth, ... Dp_setUTCFullYear, ...).\nEvery `js_CFunction` must be `unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn(J: *mut js_State)`\npassed as `Some(name)`.\n\nCRITICAL details:\n- Only the `#if defined(__unix__) || ...` / `gettimeofday` branch of the\n  `#ifdef` ladder is compiled on this platform (Linux/glibc). Translate ONLY\n  that branch (`struct timeval tv; gettimeofday(&tv, NULL); return tv.tv_sec * 1000.0 + tv.tv_usec / 1000.0;`\n  or whatever the C says exactly). Ignore the `_WIN32` branches.\n- `LocalTZA()` uses `time(NULL)`, `gmtime`, `localtime`, `mktime` — reproduce\n  exactly, including the `static double tza; static int once` caching if present.\n  `mktime` takes `*mut tm`; `gmtime`/`localtime` return `*mut tm` (a pointer to\n  a static buffer — the C code relies on that, so copy the struct where the C\n  code copies it and don't copy where it doesn't).\n- All the printf-style formatting (`fmttime`, `fmtdate`, `fmtdatetime`,\n  Dp_toISOString, ...) must use libc `snprintf`/`sprintf` from `crate::cstd`\n  with byte-identical format strings and argument lists. Do not reimplement.\n  Watch the `%02d` / `%+03d` / `%.3f`-style specifiers and the `int` casts —\n  C passes `(int)` casts of doubles: use `cvt_i32(...)` for those.\n- `sscanf`-based parsing in `parseDateTime` / `D_parse`: use libc `sscanf` from\n  crate::cstd with the identical format strings, passing `*mut c_int` /\n  `*mut f64` pointers. If the C code uses a hand-written parser instead,\n  transliterate it literally.\n- `toint`/`pmod`/`TimeClip` etc. involve double->int conversions: use `cvt_i32`\n  or `cvt_i64` per the guide.\n- `js_isdateobject` lives in `crate::json` (it is defined in json.c); if\n  jsdate.c needs it, import it from there.\n- errors: `js_rangeerror!`, `js_typeerror!` macros.\n- The month/day name tables (`\"Jan\"`, `\"Sun\"`, ...) must keep their exact\n  contents and order; use `static NAMES: [&core::ffi::CStr; N] = [c\"Jan\", ...];`\n  and `.as_ptr()` at the use site.\n- Preserve the exact order of property definitions in `jsB_initdate`.\n\nSTEP 3 — Verify: run\n`cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"jsdate\\.rs\" | head -60`\nand fix every error attributable to src/jsdate.rs. Errors in other modules\n(jsstring, jsregexp, json, jsrepr may still be missing) are expected. If the\nbuild aborts before type-checking because other modules are missing (E0583),\ncreate a THROWAWAY crate under `$TMPDIR` with stubs for the missing modules to\ntype-check your file — and delete it afterwards. Never add stub files to src/.\n\nSTEP 4 — Report the no_mangle symbols defined, line count, and remaining errors.","agentId":"a4c57014d7aa00951","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The full crate now builds cl